    "https://jobs.kingston.ac.uk/vacancy/organisational-development-ld-coordinator-620373.html": {
      "title": "Organisational Development (L&D) Co-ordinator (4967)",
      "description": "Organisational Development (L&D) Co-ordinator (4967) - Kingston University London Search this site Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ Kingston University London Search our site Share: Facebook Twitter Google+ A–Z Advanced search Search this site Site search Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Pinterest LinkedIn Google+ Snapchat Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Home > Jobs > Search for jobs Facebook Twitter Google+ Jobs: Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Joining us: About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Organisational Development (L&D) Co-ordinator Faculty/Directorate Finance, Infrastructure and Human Resources School/Function Human Resources Contract type Permanent Location of vacancy Penrhyn Road Actual hours 37 Salary from 34,687.00 Salary to 39,146.00 Posted Date 28/09/2026 Closing Date 14/10/2026 Ref No 4967 Documents Candidate Pack (PDF , 10784.32kb) Job Description (Word , 537.33kb) The Role We are seeking an enthusiastic OD Co-ordinator to join our Organisational Development team and play a key role in supporting the delivery of learning and organisational development activity across the University. Working as part of an experienced and supportive HR team, you will provide high-quality administration and co-ordination across a wide range of learning and development activities, including training, mentoring, staff engagement and induction programmes. You will help ensure learning opportunities are well organised, accessible and delivered effectively, supporting the smooth running of the University’s annual learning and development programme. As a key point of contact for managers and staff, you will provide advice and guidance on learning and development processes and procedures, coordinate training events and logistics, and maintain learning and development information on our intranet pages. You will also support online and compliance training, HR and learning systems, reporting and evaluation, as well as supplier and financial processes. The role offers the opportunity to work collaboratively with colleagues and stakeholders across the University and contribute to projects and continuous improvement activity that enhance the learning and organisational development service. The Person We’re looking for someone who is organised, proactive and customer-focused, with a genuine interest in learning and organisational development. You’ll be comfortable working across a varied workload, managing competing priorities and ensuring that learning and development activity is delivered smoothly and efficiently. You’ll have experience of working in an HR, OD or L&D environment and be confident providing advice and guidance to managers and staff. You’ll have strong administrative and organisational skills, with experience of coordinating events, maintaining accurate records and using HR or learning systems to manage and report on information. You’ll be a confident communicator who can build positive relationships with colleagues, stakeholders and external providers. You’ll enjoy working collaboratively, sharing information and supporting colleagues, while also being able to work independently and take ownership of your work. You’ll have a practical and solution-focused approach, with an eye for detail and an interest in finding ways to improve processes and services. You’ll also be comfortable working with digital and e-learning tools and using data to support reporting and decision-making. Directorate/Function The HR Function provides the strategy and infrastructure to enable Kingston University to achieve its core purpose. The successful candidate will be joining an experienced and talented team of HR professionals who deliver HR operations, strategy and design for its 3k strong employee base. The HR team works in partnership with academics and professional services staff to achieve the overall plans for the University. Our professionals give high level support across the University along with responding to day-to-day queries from all areas and staff. In addition, they ensure our policies and procedures provide suitable frameworks to enable staff to operate successfully during their employment at Kingston University. Together we aim to enable Kingston University to recruit, develop and motivate staff, so that we all contribute to the University’s success. Further information This role is advertised as a full time, permernant role with a starting salary of £34,007 per annum. Interviews will be held on the 22nd October. Please note this role requires x3 days in the office per week. Please ensure you attach a CV and supporting statement to your application. For informal enquiries please contact Kate Macgregor-Head of HR Shared Services- K.Macgregor@kingston.ac.uk Please note this role is not eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker route. Bring your true self, expertise, and passion to Kingston where we are continuing to strive to build a university where authentic inclusion and belonging is at its heart. Every one of our staff and students’ identities, backgrounds and diverse experiences makes us who we are - so harness and embrace yours by applying today. We welcome applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, LGBTQ+ communities and those with disabilities. We are a place-based organisation, proud of our location in Kingston and the civic role we play in our community. Our campuses inspire collaborative, innovative and creative communities. Being present on campus is important to us because it helps us to create a sense of belonging for both our staff and students. Therefore, staff are expected to be on campus for the majority of their working week. Candidates must be able to demonstrate their eligibility to work in the UK in accordance with the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006. Where required, this may include entry clearance or continued leave to remain under the Points Based Immigration Scheme. To apply click on ‘Apply Now’. If, for accessibility reasons, you need to apply in an alternative format, please email jobs@kingston.ac.uk or call the HR Shared Services team on 020 8417 3118. Apply for this job Send to a Friend Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Current Vacancies Register Login Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us Contact us Human Resources Second Floor Main Building Kingston University Penrhyn Road Kingston upon Thames KT1 2EE Kingston University jobs: Tel: +44 (0)20 8417 3118 Email us KUSCO jobs: Tel: +44(0)20 8417 2138 Email KUSCO Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Jobs Search for jobs Applicant advice Interviews and offer Joining us About us Why work here Your career Frequently asked questions Site menu Home Undergraduate study Postgraduate study International students Research Alumni Courses News Events Faculties and schools Services for business Giving Jobs About us How to find us Contact us Disclaimer Copyright Website accessibility Website feedback Freedom o